OHOS: keep the scrolled application and its controls visible during capture.
The compositor keeps the full-screen overlay opaque, so hide it during capture
instead of relying on a transparent hole. Create the toolbar as an independent
app window from the start: changing Qt::Tool to Qt::Window after native surface
creation does not map a new OHOS window. Detach it for the scrolling session and
raise it again after the window manager restores the settings window. Keep the
stitched preview alive as a parentless top-level window and delay the first frame
until the overlay has been removed. Qt widget regressions cover the original and
detached window surfaces, deferred presentation, and preview owner hiding.

